Upstream works
==============

Parts of this program are modified versions (translations to Rust,
restructured and extended, October 2026) of the following works:

* GROWI 1.0.4, by Andreas Gathmann, distributed under the GNU General
  Public License. https://personal.math.uni-sb.de/~agathmann/growi/
  -> crates/sc-growi (translation of the C++ sources: libgw/, math/, and
     the expression syntax of cm/expr.cc)

* admcycles, by Aaron Pixton, Johannes Schmitt, Vincent Delecroix, Jason
  van Zelm, Jonathan Zachhuber and Johannes Schwab, distributed under the
  GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
  https://gitlab.com/modulispaces/admcycles
  -> crates/sc-faber (graph.rs, kppoly.rs, taut.rs, generators.rs, socle.rs,
     dr.rs, classes.rs, witten.rs, grr.rs follow the corresponding admcycles
     modules)
  -> crates/sc-faber/tests/data/admcycles_hodge.txt (test data extracted
     from admcycles/data/hodge_data.sage, commit e1e53753: J. Schmitt,
     Z. Sun, "Computed data for Hodge integrals and Jacobian locus
     coefficients", 2026)

The following research programs, distributed publicly by their authors
without an explicit license, were ported to Rust (the algorithms and the
structure of the procedures follow the originals). They were obtained from
the public distribution pages below and are credited here, following
academic practice, as the source of those parts of this program:

* Carel Faber, "Numbers" (Maple, 2001-2004), distributed via R. Vakil's
  program page. https://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/programs/Numbers.tar
  -> crates/sc-faber (tau.rs, push.rs, hodge.rs: the procedures tau,
     pushn/push, klp/klmgn and lamb)

* Jim Bryan, "GWall" (Maple, 2002), distributed on the author's homepage.
  https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~jbryan/gwall.html
  -> crates/sc-gwall (comb.rs, gwpoint.rs, gwloop.rs, gwl.rs, and the
     branch/Ztil/Z/Y layer of pf.rs)
  The BPS inversion in pf.rs follows J. Bryan, R. Pandharipande, "BPS
  states of curves in Calabi-Yau 3-folds", Geom. Topol. 5 (2001) 287-318,
  arXiv:math/0009025.
